{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nWe arrived in Weimar at sunset, and I was straight away at Goethe’s. Riemer and Zelter were there, and the Grand Duke joined us for tea half an hour later. We sat together on the sofa and talked until nearly ten. It was a pleasant evening, though I confess my back aches from the carriage ride.\n\nThis morning, Zelter and I took Goethe’s carriage to the Grand Duke’s botanical garden at Belvedere. The collection is impressive, though the light was rather harsh for my eyes. We ate a simple lunch; the bread was good, the wine mediocre, and I paid six thalers for the pleasure. Goethe is still sharp, if a bit tired. The Grand Duke is affable but speaks in circles. I hope this letter finds you and the boys well. I have little else to report.\n\nYour husband,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795219176,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":192,"prompt_tokens":1132,"total_tokens":1324,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-FFjPnUSeHlAaXuju8nK4OAuB2k435s18","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1132,"prompt_ms":1094.661,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9670150176678446,"prompt_per_second":1034.1101034932276,"predicted_n":192,"predicted_ms":4520.897,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.66961780104712,"predicted_per_second":42.24825294626265}}